<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Do the Clippers Pay Brook Lopez $9.19m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Lopez is paid <strong>$9.19m</strong> because he is a seven footer who blocks shots and shoots three pointers, and there are very few of those at any age.</p>
<ul>
<li>He won a championship with <a href="/teams/milwaukee-bucks/">Milwaukee</a> in 2021 and has been named to an All-Defensive team.</li>
<li>He was paid <strong>$25m</strong> at Milwaukee in 2023-24, so this is about a third of that.</li>
<li>He changed his game in his thirties, going from a post scorer to one of the highest volume three point shooters among centers.</li>
<li>He turns 39 in April, which is why nobody offers him more than two years.</li>
<li>Only <strong>$8.75m</strong> of the contract was guaranteed when he signed it.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has played more NBA seasons than anyone else on this payroll.</p>

